==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈsɛlə/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈsɛlɚ/}} {{enPR|sĕl-ər}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛlə(ɹ)|s=2}}
* {{homophones|en|cellar}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|seller}}, {{m|enm|sellere}}, (also {{m|enm|siller}}, {{m|enm|sullar}}, {{m|enm|sullere}}), from {{inh|en|ang|*sellere}}, {{m|ang|*syllere}}, equivalent to {{affix|en|sell|-er}}. Cognate with {{cog|da|sælger}}, {{cog|sv|säljare}}, {{cog|is|seljari||a seller; dealer}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# Someone who [[sell]]s; a [[vendor]]; a [[clerk]].
#: ''Alisha was a '''seller''' of fine books.''
# Something which sells.
#: ''Two of the books Alisha authored had become big '''sellers'''.''
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Marianne Wiggins|authorlink=Marianne Wiggins|title=Went South|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=Delacorte Press|year=1980|page=87|isbn=0-440-09420-8|passage=Still, she sat in her chair and read it and reread it, six, seven times. She was pleased with it, she was pleased with herself. This time for sure, she said to herself. This one’s a '''seller'''. Really big.}}

